From f6853a5ac65b82279599b9ecc6dd1ef28ff9952f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:30:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show Kians SOC regardless of ev_scheduler.enabled, add
 charge-full ETA
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The car's own telemetry reads (SOC, plug, charging-active, estimated
time-to-full) lived inside _poll_ev_charging's `if not
ev_settings.enabled: return` early-exit, so they silently stopped
updating whenever the price/solar charging automation itself was
switched off — even though they're pure facts read from the car, no
write consequence, same as _poll_diagnostics's always-on stats. That's
why Kians SOC wasn't showing on the compact Dashboard tile.

Also exposes kia_uvo's own "Estimated Charge Duration" sensor (already
accounts for charge-curve tapering near full, not re-derived from
power/capacity here) as a clock-time ETA on the EV-laddning tile
("Fulladdad ~HH:MM"), shown whenever the car reports actively charging.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D9yfcLt9RHbqoZD18y9PT7
